  "notes": "Cash basis county, FY ended June 30, 2022. Governmental lines from the Total Governmental Funds column (Exhibit D, p4). Fund balance 2,628,437 -> 2,855,034; cash/investment fields left null as in FY2023-FY2025 (Balance Sheet p3 prints pooled cash 2,853,351 and designated investments 1,683, recorded in balance_sheet). Transfers 4,125 in (General) / out (Wireless 911); Component Unit 124,312 (Hospital Bond debt service paid by the hospital component unit) recorded as other_financing. Balance sheet from the governmental funds Balance Sheet (totals equal the Statement of Net Position, p1). Detail: General, Road and Inheritance Tax budget schedules (p5-8); nonmajor funds from the combining schedules (p9-11), one line per fund column (Veteran's Aid and Drug Fund had no activity). Schedule 5 (p12-14) budget pages print only fund-level receipts/disbursements totals, so nonmajor detail lines have budget_final null (Wireless 911 budget-schedule disbursements 14,126 include its transfer out 4,125; Hospital Bond budget receipts 124,312 = component unit). General Fund Taxes 1,585,960 (budget 1,577,010) split using the General column on p4. Budget schedule Federal 90,413 vs Exhibit D General Federal Grants 90,414 (rounding; both total 2,027,661). Lines with a budget but no actual omitted: General Operating Transfers (Out) budget (90,000), Road Operating Transfers In budget 300,000, Inheritance Tax Operating Transfers (Out) budget (300,000), Inheritance Tax Public Works. Inheritance Tax Capital Outlay 140,821 has no printed function, so it is plain Capital Outlay. Road 'State' and nonmajor 'Intergovernmental' kept as other state aid (not printed as highway allocation). Grants Fund 'Miscellaneous' 41,407 left other (no grantor printed). Read pages 1-14 of 14"
}
